From 4618d6dc90dda4c0914c8198e79912e68b6bd067 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Knifethrower <andersenpeters@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:29:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] render: draw faces over opaque texels without discard

Hypothesis: every solid terrain pixel goes through a shader that can discard, which on a
tile-based GPU stops depth being written early and weakens hidden-surface removal, so hidden
faces get shaded. Mali's `Early ZS updated quads` counter read 0 at low settings.

Change: the mesher already marks quads over opaque texels (OPAQUE_LAYER). `Sides` now sorts each
section's quads into two parts, those first, each with its own side buckets, and the world pass
draws the first part with `fs_solid_opaque`, which is `solid_color` without its discards. Not with
occlusion culling, flat draws, a shader pack's terrain or distant tiles, which keep one list.

Number that should move: `Early ZS updated quads` above 0, fragment cycles per frame down, frame
rate up, picture the same. Falsified if the counter stays 0 or a pixel changes.

Measured on an R36S at 1 GB (Mali-G31, low settings, render distance 2, a frozen world, the same
spot, about 400 MHz GPU at 76-80 C):

                          before       after
  frame rate              13.5-14.6    15.8-17.3 fps
  Early ZS updated quads  0            about 53,000 per frame
  fragment cycles         17.3 M       about 11.8 M per frame
  GPU cycles              22.9 M       about 17 M per frame
  screenshot                           0 of 307,200 pixels differ

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
